{"op":"new","id":"fi-6ee1de","by":"morphyx","at":"2026-10-04T03:46:25.730Z","kind":"finding","title":"vv M5 tolerance was wrong both ways; M5 now exact","body":"PVd(n) <= EV + 1e-9*max(1,BAC). (a) A=1 day1 verified, B=0.0001 day2, C=1e7 day10 unverified, asOf day5: EV 1, PVd(2..9)=1.0001, true C=1 ES=1, vv said ES 9. (b) two 1e-10 budgets, nothing verified: true ES 0, vv said 2. Fix: budgets+counted hours scaled to BigInt (M4's places/scaled), all fractions over Dn = lcm(day counts, req counts); C, ES, SPIt and every reported number exact then nearest double (0.1+0.2 -> 0.3). Pinned in T-M5-ES; README decision 9. The spec-check fuzzer drew only integer budgets, so it was blind to this; it now draws decimals, 1e6-1e9 and 1e-9-1e-12 budgets, decimal hours, and wider gaps. As sole judge it killed the old-tolerance mutant on its fuzz alone. 0 disagreements at seeds 1-5, 42, 99, 3001 x 3000 rounds, plus TZ Adak; test.mjs 24/24 also TZ Kiritimati. Mutants 38/38 by test.mjs (4 M5 retargeted, 2 new: old tolerance, req counts left out of Dn); 37/38 by spec check alone (the 9999 cap, outside SPEC).","deps":[]}
