{"op":"note","id":"ta-1d4849","by":"modulo","at":"2026-10-04T19:39:58.139Z","text":"Built (Modulo): enclosure/gen.mjs writes 5 parts (lid, body, baffle, collar, pod) plus ref/ (back-air, driver-bound, stack.json). measure.mjs builds each in Truck: all watertight, max 190 mm; nest 90x65 (1.0 per side); back air 302.8 minus 33.0 driver bound = 269.8 cm3; 151 holes of 3.5 mm = 1452.8 mm2, all inside the collar front chamber; check.mjs --clearance 1 on the stack: nearest 3.0 mm. test.mjs 21/21, vv 17/18 (RANGE unverified until the hour of polls). Enclosure mutants 10/10 (shelf/tape1-enc-mutants.json with enclosure/test-geom.mjs). Needs someone else to reproduce and close."}
{"op":"new","id":"fi-03abd5","by":"modulo","at":"2026-10-04T19:39:58.165Z","kind":"finding","title":"Truck cannot cut a pocket into a plate that already has a through-hole loop","body":"baffle as one cup (outline + driver-hole loop, extruded 9, pocket cut from z=3) failed: 'This shell is not oriented and closed'. A plain cup with no hole loop builds fine. Workaround: split into two pure even-odd extrudes (baffle plate + collar ring). Also: Truck volumes of polygon-tessellated solids are off by ~1e-5 relative (pod cavity 302.773 vs exact 302.7675 cm3; driver cylinder 32.993 vs pi*20.5^2*25 = 33.006, i.e. the bound reads 13 mm3 LOW, the unsafe side, irrelevant against a 69.8 cm3 margin).","deps":[]}
{"op":"new","id":"de-fe2a29","by":"modulo","at":"2026-10-04T19:39:58.190Z","kind":"decision","title":"Enclosure layout: nest left, speaker pod beside it (not under), sealed by baffle + collar under the lid","body":"The grille needs more open area (1257 mm2) than a 40 mm driver face can carry with holes under 4 mm and printable webs, so the grille is wider (r 33) than the driver. Holes outside the driver would vent the box interior, i.e. the back of the cone. Hence a front chamber: a collar between baffle and lid, and every hole is checked to lie inside it. The pod sits beside the nest so the driver magnet is never over the antenna. nestFloor 2 mm and the 3.5 mm/4.8 mm grille are provisional; the hour of polls decides the first. NOT modelled: the PN532 board's outline and mount, the DevKit's standoffs, buttons/pot bodies below the lid (their holes are placed clear of the pod by arithmetic only), screws/fastening of pod to baffle (silicone assumed).","deps":[]}
{"op":"done","id":"ta-1d4849","by":"morphyx","at":"2026-10-04T19:47:45.688Z","evidence":"Reproduced by Morphyx (turn 3): node enclosure/test-geom.mjs -> enclosure ok; node shelf/mutants.mjs . shelf/tape1-enc-mutants.json enclosure/test-geom.mjs -> 10/10 caught; test.mjs 22/22; vv no problems, 17/18 (RANGE unverified until the hour, as it should be). Wording revised: 'over the antenna, nothing conductive between' moved from NEST to RANGE, since the model holds no reader board (fi below)."}
{"op":"new","id":"fi-1083e4","by":"morphyx","at":"2026-10-04T19:47:45.716Z","kind":"finding","title":"TAPE-ENC-NEST was verified for a clause the model can't hold: 'over the antenna'","body":"The lid model has no PN532 board, and refs/tape gives no outline or antenna position (parts.json only says generic red V3 modules differ in antenna tuning). So T-E-NEST could verify the pocket but not the antenna under it. Moved that clause into TAPE-ENC-RANGE, whose acceptance now asks for the board mounted where its antenna was measured on the board in hand. The same hour of polls that sets the debounce also sets the mount. Same shape as fi-c224bf: a pass that reads as covering more than it looked at.","deps":[]}
{"op":"new","id":"ta-8652f4","by":"morphyx","at":"2026-10-04T19:47:45.743Z","kind":"task","title":"Lid: reader-board mount as a parameter (antenna centre x,y, board outline, standoff height) filled from calipers on the household's board","body":"Wave-1 parts get ordered before the print. When the board arrives, measure it; gen.mjs takes the numbers into P, measure.mjs checks the antenna centre sits under the nest centre within a tolerance and no screw or standoff lies within the loop's footprint. Until then the mount stays unmodelled, and RANGE stays unverified.","deps":[]}
