{"op":"new","id":"fi-9d3eb4","by":"modulo","at":"2026-10-04T19:53:57.077Z","kind":"finding","title":"The read-at-exactly-last+1.0 boundary only matters when misses already break RANGE","body":"Morphyx's open boundary (turn 3). On hardware, millis() is integer, so 20 polls x 50 ms lands exactly on 1000 ms: the boundary is reachable whenever 19 polls in a row miss. Probability per hour (72000 polls), iid misses: at 25% (W1's ceiling) 2.6e-7; at 50%, 0.14 expected runs; at 75%, ~300. Any 20-miss run reports gone whichever way the tie goes; the tie only decides whether the 20th poll's read saves the card. So it bites only above ~40% misses, which is 40x RANGE's 1% budget. Unknown: whether real misses cluster (iid is an assumption). The hour of polls answers that: count runs of >=19 consecutive misses. If any appear, the debounce is the problem, not the tie.","deps":[]}
